hart</surname><given-names>GM</given-names></name><name><surname>Armour</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Duncan</surname><given-names>JL</given-names></name><name><surname>Dunn</surname><given-names>AM</given-names></name><name><surname>Jennings</surname><given-names>FW</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Veterinary parasitology</article-title><source>Longman, Essex</source><year>1987</year></citation></ref><ref id="B34"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wall</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Shearer</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><source>Veterinary entomology</source><year>1997</year><publisher-name>Chapman &#x00026; Hall, London</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B35"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Webster</surname><given-names>RM</given-names></name><name><surname>Bugby</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><source>Light spot and fleck grain defects of economic importance to the UK leather industry, part 1, identification of causal agent. Laboratory report 184</source><year>1990</year><publisher-name>British Leather Confederation, Northampton</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B36"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Zerba</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Insecticidal activity of pyrethroids on insects of medical importance</article-title><source>Parasit Today</source><year>1988</year><volume>4</volume><fpage>53</fpage><lpage>57</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/0169-4758(88)90079-8</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>